🔹 Program 3: Unary Minus Operator Overloading

📌 Description

This program demonstrates unary operator overloading in C++.

The unary minus ("-") operator is overloaded for a user-defined "Number" class so that an object can be negated using the expression "-object".

🎯 Concept Used

Unary Operator Overloading

💡 Key Point

The expression:

"-first"

internally calls:

"first.operator-()"

This allows operators to work with objects of user-defined classes.
